From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:50:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: report raw frame in first kernel fault record

DDR3 CPU_COMM IRQ trials stop reporting after the fault-address line,
before the ESR decoder and normal Oops register dump. Emit raw PC, LR,
SP, ESR and initial argument registers in that same first record so the
faulting access can be identified from UART even when later reporting
cannot progress. No pointer dereference, symbol lookup, delay or change
to fault handling is added. This improves diagnosis; it is not a fix for
the underlying corruption and does not qualify IRQ operation.

--- a/arch/arm64/mm/fault.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/mm/fault.c
@@ -301,8 +301,16 @@
 {
 	bust_spinlocks(1);
 
-	pr_alert("Unable to handle kernel %s at virtual address %016lx\n", msg,
-		 addr);
+	/* Keep the raw frame in the first record: on a corrupted kernel,
+	 * later ESR/page-table/stack reporting may itself stop progressing.
+	 */
+	pr_alert("Unable to handle kernel %s at virtual address %016lx "
+		 "pc=%016llx lr=%016llx sp=%016llx esr=%016lx "
+		 "x0=%016llx x1=%016llx x2=%016llx x3=%016llx "
+		 "x4=%016llx x5=%016llx x6=%016llx x7=%016llx\n",
+		 msg, addr, regs->pc, regs->regs[30], regs->sp, esr,
+		 regs->regs[0], regs->regs[1], regs->regs[2], regs->regs[3],
+		 regs->regs[4], regs->regs[5], regs->regs[6], regs->regs[7]);
 
 	kasan_non_canonical_hook(addr);
 
